cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the cached data, please cite the archived release."
title: "Tactical cash reserve versus dollar-cost averaging: backtest code and cached data (Taiwan 0050, United States SPY)"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible backtest of a tactical cash reserve rule against investing every
  periodic contribution immediately. The rule diverts a fixed share of each
  contribution into an interest-bearing reserve and deploys the reserve in full
  the first time the market closes 15 percent or more below its trailing 52-week
  high. One market-agnostic engine, one set of fixed parameters and one code path
  are applied to Taiwan (Yuanta Taiwan Top 50 ETF, 0050) and the United States
  (SPDR S&P 500 ETF Trust, SPY) over 2 January 2009 to 3 August 2026. The archive
  contains the documented companion notebook, the cached total-return price series
  and savings-deposit rate series with their raw sources, the publication figure
  scripts, and a probability of backtest overfitting (CSCV) analysis at 10, 16 and
  20 blocks.
